THE TRANSIT DATA IS NOT COVERED BY THIS LICENCE.

The MIT grant above applies to the source code in this repository and to
nothing else. No transit data is redistributed here — the feeds are downloaded
at runtime from each agency, and `data/` is git-ignored precisely so that this
stays true.

If you run this, you are consuming those feeds directly and their terms apply
to you rather than to me:

  * AAATA/TheRide grant a "limited, nonexclusive, non-assignable,
    nontransferable, revocable license" for the purpose of assisting transit
    riders or promoting public transportation. It requires displaying the
    notice below prominently wherever their data appears, refreshing the GTFS
    within three business days of a new publication, and not using their logos
    or other intellectual property. "Nontransferable" is why the ZIPs are not
    committed to this repository.

        Transit scheduling, geographic, and real-time data provided by
        permission of AAATA/TheRide.

  * University of Michigan Transit Services publish MBus data through the
    Mobility Database and Transitland without a stated restriction.

TheRide's realtime endpoints are undocumented and appear in no feed registry;
see docs/feeds.md for how they were found and why anything depending on them
must degrade gracefully. Treat them as a courtesy, not a contract.

Map tiles are © OpenFreeMap and © OpenMapTiles, from OpenStreetMap data
© OpenStreetMap contributors, under the Open Database License.
